The function makes the same calls in the same order: `GetNumSubFields()`, then `GetSubField(subFieldIndex)` only when the index is in range, otherwise `GetScale()`. Behavior is therefore unchanged. Without seeing those virtual implementations I can't make a bigger change safely, so this is only a small rewrite.

- It tests the common in-range case first.
- It binds the result as a const pointer and returns `1.0` explicitly for a null subfield.
- Any speedup will be small at best. The real cost is likely in the virtual calls, which this keeps.

```cpp
FIT_FLOAT64 FieldBase::GetScale(const FIT_UINT16 subFieldIndex) const
{
    if (subFieldIndex < GetNumSubFields())
    {
        const auto subfield = GetSubField(subFieldIndex);
        if (NULL != subfield)
            return subfield->scale;
        return 1.0;
    }

    return GetScale();
}
```